# Platform Date

Minimal example of a **platform-constructible** host type: Schema uses bare
`Date` once Target declares `Date::CONSTRUCT` in `%requires`. Construction
writes `[:Date …]`.

Haxe’s `Date` constructor needs all six ints
`(year, month, day, hour, min, sec)`; month is **0-based** (December = 11).
Methods use real Haxe names (`getFullYear`).

## Schema

```
Person = String/name Date/dob
```

## Construction

```
[:Person "Ada" [:Date 1815 11 10 0 0 0]]
```

## Methods

```
Person::bornYear = { dob.getFullYear() }

Person::caption = {
  y = this.bornYear().
  name.concat(" born ").concat(y.str())
}

Person::withDob = { Int/y, Int/m, Int/d |
  [:Person name [:Date y m d 0 0 0]]
}
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%requires
Date
Date::CONSTRUCT(Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int) -> Date
Date::getFullYear() -> Int

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    var p = PersonAssemblage.factory();
    wchntConsole.println(p.caption());
    wchntConsole.println(p.toConstruction(0, helper));
}
```

Pretty-print shows `%instanceOfDate`, not a fake `[:Date …]` round-trip
(ctor args cannot be recovered from a live host value).

Live twin: `live-examples/platform_date.wcn` (`%cli-live`, JS `Date`).
